<br/>You can expect ~10% healing from the two bonuses combined. If you are wearing your Phase 1 tier set you can swap off it as soon as you get 2 pieces of the new tier.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/creatureportrait_twilightshammer_dragonegg_01.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Restoration Druid Trinkets in Phase 3</span></h2>Phase 3 trinkets are substantially more interesting than in Phase 1/<wbr/>2 since they use a new proc system that doesn't have an "internal cooldown". Instead, your trinkets should just proc at random times throughout the fight. There are also a lot of trinkets that proc healing now instead of just stats.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94530/lightning-imbued-chalice">
