<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Restoration Druids</span></h2>We don't require any hit rating due to our <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=84736/natures-focus">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_staff_90.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nature's Focus</span></a> talent which gives us hit cap for free.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_uncut_purple.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Gemming for Restoration Druids</span></h2>In Phase 1 we gemmed to maximize socket bonuses and intellect. As the expansion goes on, pure secondary gems will rise in value relative to intellect gems. In Phase 3, freshly geared characters can continue the intellect-focused gem strategy but geared characters (520+ ilvl) can start considering pure secondary gems. <b>The difference between these two gem sets is small.</b>
