<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafting-professions">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Professions &amp; Crafted Gear for Restoration Druids</span></h2>Professions are quite close in Mists of Pandaria and any two crafting professions will get you pretty close to optimal.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="engineering">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_engineering.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Engineering for Restoration Druids</h4>Engineering is a great profession because of the sheer number of advantages offered.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=126731/synapse-springs">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Synapse Springs</span></a> is an enchant you attach to your Gloves that gives you a big on-use Intellect boost. They average out to the same amount of Intellect as other professions but are much burstier.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">You get a very good pre-raid helm in <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77535/camouflage-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Camouflage Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Camouflage Retinal Armor</span></a> - a special helm that you can socket with two secondaries of your choice. Keep in mind though that it's replaced much faster in phase 3.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">While somewhat less useful on Resto Druid, <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=55016/nitro-boosts">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nitro Boosts</span></a> lets you sprint for a few seconds.</div></li></ul>Overall, Engineering just offers a lot and is a locked-in profession for most specs.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="leatherworking">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_leatherworking.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Leatherworking for Restoration Druids</h4>Leatherworking gives you an early intellect enchant in <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=124552/fur-lining-intellect">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_pelt_11.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fur Lining - Intellect</span></a>. You also get <a class="q2 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=29530/drums-of-speed">
<img alt="Drums of Speed" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_drum_04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Drums of Speed</span></a> which is a powerful utility button to gain. You get the same stat bonuses as other professions but stronger utility items than most.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="alchemy">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_alchemy.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Alchemy for Restoration Druids</h4>Alchemy offers a strong pre-raid trinket in <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=75274/zen-alchemist-stone">
<img alt="Zen Alchemist Stone" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pet_scorchedstone.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Zen Alchemist Stone</span></a> and a flat 320 Intellect whenever we drink a flask. We can also get this out in the world by using <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=75525/alchemists-flask">
<img alt="Alchemist's Flask" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_endlesspotion.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Alchemist's Flask</span></a> so you'll never be without your stat bonus. Alchemy offers great quality-of-life.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="blacksmithing">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_blacksmithing.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Blacksmithing for Restoration Druids</h4>Blacksmithing gives you two extra sockets: <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=55628/socket-bracer">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/item_socketedbracer.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Socket Bracer</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=55641/socket-gloves">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_addsocketglove.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Socket Gloves</span></a>, which offers a level of flexibility that other professions can lack. You're also getting the power without any strings which is very nice - the sockets can go on any piece of gear in the appropriate slots.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Crafted Gear for Restoration Druids</span></h3>Most crafted items are no longer restricted by profession which means we're able to wear leatherworking crafted items even if we aren't leatherworkers.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="phase-3-crafts-high-level-might-be-expensive">Phase 3 Crafts (High level, might be expensive)</h4>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94273/spirit-keeper-footguards">
<img alt="Spirit Keeper Footguards" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boot_leather_raidmonk_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Spirit Keeper Footguards</span></a> (Leatherworking - requires a Raid material).</div></li>
